## Worksheet

**F1 (Core loop):** GameState class = single state object; SeededRandom seeds all rng.next()/range() calls; endTurn() calls processProduction→processNeeds→processMorale→processStorm→processRepairs→processCaravan→processEvents in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 (Map):** generateMap() builds 8x8 grid from seeded rng; canBuild() checks terrain===required. No adjacency-bonus code found anywhere. Score 1.

**F3 (Economy):** mine produces ore, smelter consumes ore+power→metal (real chain); storageMax caps enforced with overflow logging in processProduction. Score 2.

**F4 (Population):** colonists have skill/fatigue/morale/assigned fields, but processProduction's skillBonus uses only `c.level`, never `c.skill`; fatigue is written (+20/turn) but never read by production. Score 1.

**F5 (Needs):** processNeeds consumes food/water, drops morale -20 on shortage, processMorale recovers +10/turn (not instant loss) — but morale is never read in processProduction. Score 1.

**F6 (Research):** 8 nodes defined; canResearch() checks prereq (only 'automation' actually has one) and cost deducted in doResearch(); `node.effects` objects are set but never read anywhere else in the code. Score 1.

**F7 (Events):** 10 distinct events present; selection is uniform rng.range(), not weighted; showEventModal() only ever creates a single "OK" button — no 2-3 choice branches exist for any event; eventCooldown tracked via turn threshold. Score 1.

**F8 (Trade):** goods array in renderTrade() is fully hardcoded (buy/sell/stock same every render, ignores game.resources); buyGood/sellGood do mutate scrip and resources correctly. Score 1.

**F9 (Hazard):** processStorm() damages buildings with severity scaling with turn; healthMul in processProduction reduces output for damaged buildings; processRepairs spends parts to reduce damage — but shield building's `mitigation` field and research `stormMitigation` effect are never read anywhere. Score 1.

**F10 (Save/load):** save() serializes full state to JSON string (clipboard-copyable); GameState.load() parses, throws on bad input, caught and alerted via loadBtn.onclick. Score 2.

**F11 (End conditions):** checkWin()/checkLose() both called after every endTurn(), both reachable; getScore() combines population/research/resources/turns; showEndScreen() renders summary modal. Score 2.

**F12 (UI):** tab-btn click handlers toggle .active; log entries show `[Turn ${entry.turn}]`; tile/tree-node tooltips show cost/produce/consume; keydown handler wires Space+1-6; @media(max-width:600px) adjusts layout. Score 2.

**F13 (Dev panel):** runTests() checks real invariants (storage caps, research prereqs, save/load round-trip, damage bounds); runBenchmark() runs 200 headless endTurn() calls and prints stateHash(). Score 2.

**G1:** research node `.effects` fields set in initResearch() but never read by processProduction/processStorm/etc. Score 0.

**G2:** processNeeds shortage → col.morale -=20 (real state change) → but morale never referenced in processProduction's output formula. Score 1.

**G3:** processStorm damages buildings → healthMul in processProduction cuts output → processRepairs spends parts and reduces damage, restoring output next turn — full pipeline wired every relevant turn. Score 4.

**G4:** renderTrade's goods array has static hardcoded buy/sell prices, never reads game.resources or any drift variable. Score 0.

**G5:** showEventModal() only builds one "OK" button per event; no event offers branching choices to mutate state differently. Score 0.

